{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 32, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 32, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=33&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=31&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 647532822, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r647532822-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Amazing things in pashupatinath I haven’t seen before ", "text": " It is a holy place , but the main temple is not open for non Hindu people.  It is under world h heritage site. There is a holy river near by the temple.Interesting thing is that people are burnt here after their death.  If you are once here you should not forget to visit here.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C49562BF3D4CF5FB8739091B91F35D3B", "name": "Alejandro Ramos", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/alejandroramus", "username": "alejandroramus", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/30/8a/fc/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 3, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 298199, "location_name": "Osaka Prefecture", "location_name_detailed": "Osaka Prefecture, Japan"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/30/9f/93/photo0jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-01-22", "published_at_date": "2019-01-22"}, {"review_id": 647495611, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r647495611-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "one of the World heritage site of nepal", "text": "Pashupatinath is a temple of lord shiva, hindu religion. a really nice place to visit, its better to go in the early morning and evening for the nice views. covering with nature. highly recommended!!!!!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "79F9C2E1B35AD9BC0D34432D58402D16", "name": "Yusuke Harada", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/322yusukeh", "username": "322yusukeh", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/17/d7/f5/97/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 7, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1066451, "location_name": "Minato", "location_name_detailed": "Minato, Japan"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-01-22", "published_at_date": "2019-01-22"}, {"review_id": 647493729, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r647493729-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A must visit for the spiritually/ religion inclined", "text": "Har Har Mahadev.\n\nForeigners can give this a miss. I believe foreigners have to pay an amount to enter the temple and can go only till a particular section. Under the imposition of such condition, better not to visit.\n\nVery dusty around. Lot of construction going on. Wouldn't have gone to the temple if I wasn't devout. From parking area to the temple, one needs to walk atleast 700 meters. It was difficult for my elderly parents but somehow they made it.\n\nWasn't harassed by pandas/ priests like how it happens in Indian temples. Neither is the temple area as dirty compared to temples back home in India. Went around 2pm, so I guess wasn't too crowded. Cannot even see the Shivalinga properly as they didn't turn on the lights inside the sanctum sanctorum.\n\nHowever there was a sense of achievement after visiting the temple. Guess us Hindus feel that way upon completion of a pilgrimage.\n\nActually did not have the visit in my itinerary as was not intending to stay in Kathmandu. But missed my flight to Pokhara.. So decided to go to the temple in the evening. But when I reached, the temple was closed. God wasn't interested to have me I guess. On my way back, I again tried to have darshan and was successful.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2019-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "D3A21F615A0FC62B1CF2FC0A91065D10", "name": "amit1008", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/amit1008", "username": "amit1008", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e2/11/default-avatar-2020-41.jpg", "contribution_count": 21, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 294265, "location_name": "Singapore", "location_name_detailed": "Singapore, Singapore"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-01-22", "published_at_date": "2019-01-22"}, {"review_id": 646584875, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r646584875-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "For soul", "text": "This is the place where you can find most amazing spiritual experiences. Friendly people with rich culture", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "881203D2CC8199D1BC075686EBC33A81", "name": "Ramachandran R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/160ramachandranr", "username": "160ramachandranr", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/41/0a/2a/rama-c.jpg", "contribution_count": 2, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 298570, "location_name": "Kuala Lumpur", "location_name_detailed": "Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-01-17", "published_at_date": "2019-01-17"}, {"review_id": 646492808, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r646492808-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "The Temple with a difference", "text": "The temple is unique ....with 4 sides thrown open for devotees to have a good look at the Lord .....the priests are kind but the main thing which draws me is the burning ghat behind it.....and the small pieces of wood each old man and woman gets to work at outside the temple area so that there is never any dearth of wood for cremations . It is a unique culture and it works efficiently ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2018-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "CB28EB99A3E58BF8C5637EA769C1E738", "name": "Sightsee611662", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Sightsee611662", "username": "Sightsee611662", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/03/58/c4/sightsee611662.jpg", "contribution_count": 91, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304558, "location_name": "Kolkata (Calcutta)", "location_name_detailed": "Kolkata (Calcutta), India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-01-17", "published_at_date": "2019-01-17"}, {"review_id": 646331145, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r646331145-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "the shiva temple", "text": "on the bank of dirty bagmati river.\nin the centre of the city, old, crowded, non-managed,guarded by armed personnel, filthywith mile long cue of believers and stray monkeys and shiva in dark, damp, sacred interior of the temple of world famous nepalese architecture with intricate woodwork lattices.\nhowever the enchanted devotees will not allow you to stand still and appreciate the main temple's architecture by jostling for view of the god.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-12-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "BCA632FC536D295F6D2ADF451697ECEE", "name": "ghosal_rg", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ghosal_rg", "username": "ghosal_rg", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f6/0d/default-avatar-2020-34.jpg", "contribution_count": 167, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 644044, "location_name": "Durgapur", "location_name_detailed": "Durgapur, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-01-16", "published_at_date": "2019-01-16"}, {"review_id": 646239109, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r646239109-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Powerful Prevedic temple", "text": "A powerful temple with vibrant energy. It is one of the Prevedic temples with Shiva in the form of Pashupathi (one who had conquered the animal nature within oneself/ Lord of all animals). Whenever you visit this temple don't forget to visit the Guheshwori temple with in the temple complex. Behind the temple along the banks of Bhagmati River I saw many deadbodies being burned which reminded me of Kashi.There are hundreds of small Shiva temples within the complex. The place is at the same time beautiful, peaceful and powerful. Must visit.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "F870715510CC605D37FFB0B5DAF1DFDC", "name": "Dhanya D", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/DhanyaD31", "username": "DhanyaD31", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/1d/97/d3/dhanyad31.jpg", "contribution_count": 6, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1102838, "location_name": "Hosur", "location_name_detailed": "Hosur, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-01-16", "published_at_date": "2019-01-16"}, {"review_id": 646229703, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r646229703-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "nice place", "text": "It was very nice and beautiful place to visit,specially in evening time . Because in the evening time the view is very nice coz of lights. specially for hindu people it was very nice temple to pray. there is big statute of lord Shiva.   ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2019-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "FDB66691917E2E26554F07DEEC801AEC", "name": "Susan V", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/susanvL5267NB", "username": "susanvL5267NB", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn